.TH LAUNCHCTL 1 "November 2026" "vultureOS" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
launchctl \- talk to the launch daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B launchctl
.I subcommand
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B launchctl
asks
.B vlaunchd
about the jobs it looks after, and tells it what to do with them. Everything but
.B list
takes root.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIlabel\fR]
With no label, a line for every job: its process, how it last ended, and its label. With one, what's known about that job.
.TP
.B start \fIlabel
Starts a job that's loaded, now.
.TP
.B stop \fIlabel
Asks a job to stop. If it's kept alive, it comes back.
.TP
.B load \fIpath
Loads a job from a property list.
.TP
.B unload \fIpath
Stops a job and forgets it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if it worked. 113 if there's no such job, and 1 for anything else.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR launchd.plist (5)
